---
description: Testing conventions
globs: "**/test/**,**/tests/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

Flutter: use flutter_test + mocktail + riverpod_test. Mock repositories at
the provider boundary — never hit a real network in a test. Override
providers via ProviderScope overrides, not global state mutation.

Backend: use pytest. Unit test service.py by mocking repository.py.
Integration tests for router.py use a test database (sqlite in-memory or a
disposable test Postgres) — never run tests against a real staging/prod
database or external API.

Every new Failure subtype or FailureCode needs a corresponding equality/
mapping test. Every new repository method needs a test proving transport
exceptions are mapped to Failure and never leaked.
